# === OS Memory Area (21-999) ===
# --- OS Variables (21-99) ---
21 0        # Current thread ID (0 = OS)
22 10        # Number of active threads
23 0        # Scheduler state (0=init, 1=running)
24 0        # System timer/cycle counter
25 0        # Context switch counter
26 0        # Blocked thread counter
27 1        # Next thread to check (for round-robin) - start with thread 1
28 0        # Temp for saving registers during context switch
29 0        # Temp for calculations
30 0        # Thread search counter
31 11       # Maximum number of threads (0 - 10 included) 
32 80       # Thread entry size
33 100      # Thread base offset
34 0        # Last thread execution start 
35 0        # Instruction count of the last executed thread

# --- Thread Table (100-979) ---
# Thread structure (80 bytes each):
# Offset 0: Thread ID
# Offset 1: State (1=READY, 2=RUNNING, 3=BLOCKED, 4=HALTED)
# Offset 2: PC
# Offset 3: SP
# Offset 4: First execution time (when thread first ran)
# Offset 5: Last start time (when last context switched to)
# Offset 6: Total executed instructions
# Offset 7: IC of the last executed instruction
# Offset 8: Block duration (for BLOCKED threads)
# Offset 9-79: Reserved for future use

# Thread 0 (OS) - 100-179
100 0       # Thread ID = 0 (OS)
101 2       # State = RUNNING
102 21      # PC (OS start)
103 19999   # SP
104 0       # First execution time 
105 0       # Last start time [USED TO TRACK 34 - 35 means total thread usage]
106 0       # Total executed instructions [Total OS usagae]
107 0       # IC of the last executed instruction  [NOT USED FOR OS THREAD]
108 0       # Block duration
# 109-179 Reserved

# This tables will be initiliazed by the OS
